# MadGraph5 batch script: p3 r3 > p3 r3 NP<=2
# in vibegraph_toy_color_UFO, restricted by restrict_k6.dat.
#
# Why this exact process:
#   The sextet Clebsch coefficients K6 and K6Bar, which this crate's colour
#   grammar refuses outright, reached through an s-channel sextet diquark. The
#   sextet is internal, so the pair reduces through
#   K6(m,i,j) K6Bar(m,k,l) = (T(l,i)T(k,j) + T(k,i)T(l,j))/2 before any colour
#   matrix is built and no external leg ever carries two colour lines -- which
#   separates the reduction rules from the open question of how a sextet leg is
#   written into an event file.
#
# The model path is repo-relative to the vendored UFO; build.sh rewrites it to
# the work-area copy it stages under output/models/. This model is ours, so its
# restrict cards live inside the model directory and are staged with it.
#
# `display interactions` prints the count MadGraph's own interaction splitting
# arrives at (one interaction per coupling-order tuple, import_ufo.add_interaction)
# into the build log, which is where extract_interactions.py reads it from.
#
# The order bound is explicit because the model declares no coupling at all under
# the QCD order MadGraph's WEIGHTED search reads by name.
import model validation/ufo/vibegraph_toy_color_UFO-k6
display interactions
generate p3 r3 > p3 r3 NP<=2
output p3r3_to_p3r3_toy_sextet -nojpeg
launch
set lpp1 0
set lpp2 0
set ebeam1 250
set ebeam2 250
set use_syst False
done
